-- The questions the semantic fixture asks, of a file that is halfway through being edited.
--
-- What M7 buys is that this file has answers at all: the declarations below a broken one still
-- parse, so the index still holds them, and the resolver says nothing further about what the
-- parser already reported. The diagnostics section at the top of the .expect is the second half of
-- that - one message per mistake, and every one of them from the parser.

import Shapes

-- A function whose body has not been typed yet.
fn halfWritten(s: Shape) -> Int:

-- A `match` whose alternatives have not been typed yet. The pivot is still what an editor is asked
-- about while they are being written.
fn pending(s: Shape) -> Int = match s:
--                                  ^pivot

-- A declaration that got as far as its name.
data Colour

-- A binding whose `| match:` alternatives have not been typed yet. Without the poisoned
-- alternative the parser writes in their place, the resolver would tell a half-typed line that its
-- refutable pattern needs the alternatives that are being typed.
fn probe(s: Shape) -> Int:
    let Circle(c) = s | match:

    return c.radius
--         ^bound

-- Everything after all of that still resolves.
fn twice(s: Shape) -> Int = area(s) + area(s)
--                          ^classfun

fn main() -> Int:
    let c = Shapes.Circle {radius: 4}
--                 ^con
    return twice(c)
--         ^call
